    "# HASTS206 Applied Demographic Analysis: Assignment 2\n",
    "**University of Zimbabwe, Department of Mathematics and Computational Sciences**\n",
    "\n",
    "> **All figures in this notebook are HYPOTHETICAL.** The data are synthetic and the district labels are illustrative.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to run:** place the original CSVs in `data/`, then run all cells from the repository root (`Kernel > Restart & Run All`). All paths are relative. Outputs consumed by Power BI are written to `outputs/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Section | Content |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 0 | Setup and data-quality log |\n",
    "| 1 | Population structure and mortality (pyramids, ratios, balance, rates, abridged life table) |\n",
    "| 2 | Population projections (arithmetic, geometric, cohort-component, sensitivity) |\n",
    "| 3 | Three-state continuous-time Markov model (H, I, D) |\n",
    "| 4 | District clustering (k-means) |\n",
    "| 5 | Exports for Power BI, reconciliation figures |\n",
    "| 6 | What-if cell for the recorded presentation |\n",
    "\n",
    "Each block of code is followed by a **Notes** cell that interprets what was just executed."
   ]
  },
