  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Notes: reconciliation and the deaths scope difference.**\n",
    "- For all 24 districts, P(2025) + births - deaths + arrivals - departures equals the reported 1 January 2026 population exactly (gap = 0 persons), and births, arrivals and departures in `districts.csv` equal the sums over `age_sex.csv`.\n",
    "- **Deaths do not reconcile, by design.** `baseline_deaths_2025` covers only residents present on 1 January 2025, classified by age at baseline. District deaths add the deaths among babies born during 2025, who are not in the baseline population. The gap is therefore the implied number of deaths among 2025 births (621 in total, about 1.20 per 100 births). Using baseline deaths in a balancing equation would leave the 2026 reconstruction short by exactly that amount."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Population structure and mortality\n",
    "### 1(a) Selecting two contrasting districts, pyramids and dependency ratios\n",
