   "source": [
    "**Notes: life-table construction.** m_x is deaths over person-years. For the closed intervals, q_x = n m_x / (1 + (n - a_x) m_x) uses the supplied a_x (1.2 for ages 0-4, where deaths are concentrated early, and 2.5 elsewhere). The final interval has q = 1, so d_85+ = l_85 and L_85+ = l_85 / m_85+. Mortality rises steeply with age, from m = 0.0006 at 10-14 to 0.141 at 85+. The 0-4 band has a relatively high m_x (0.0080), reflecting infant and child mortality."
   ]
