    "**Notes: interpretation and checks.**\n",
    "- **Life expectancy at birth e0 = 73.11 years**: a hypothetical newborn would live 73.1 years on average if the 2025-style mortality rates in this schedule stayed constant (a *period* measure, pooled across sexes, not a forecast).\n",
    "- **e65 = 18.10 years**: those who reach 65 can expect to live a further 18.1 years, i.e. to about 83.1 on average. Only 76.2% of births survive to 65. Survivors to 65 can expect to die at about 83.1, well above e0 = 73.1, because e0 averages in deaths in infancy and mid-life that 65-year-olds have already survived.\n",
    "- **Numerical checks:** (1) the sum of d_x equals the radix 100,000; (2) T_0 equals the sum of L_x; (3) for the 5-year bands with a_x = 2.5, L_x equals the trapezium rule 2.5(l_x + l_x+5); (4) e_85+ equals 1/m_85+ (7.092 years). All hold to machine precision."
   ]
